{"body":"A malformed nonblank Total cell in the maturity worksheet previously became zero and silently removed exposure from the WAL input. Numeric conversion errors now raise ExposureMaturityScheduleError with the worksheet name, row, Total column and cell address. Blank totals and valid accounting values retain their existing behavior.\n\nCloses #1063\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Propagate malformed maturity amount errors with source cell context.\n- [x] Exercise real XLSX files through the parser and public WAL boundary.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py -q` — 20 passed, including `test_invalid_nonblank_total_raises`.\n- [x] Malformed text, booleans, NaN/Infinity text, overflow text and percent text raise before WAL returns a result. Errors identify row 15 and Total column 6 (F15).\n- [x] Blank cells remain zero; currency, grouped and parenthesized accounting values retain their amounts; a valid workbook produces WAL 52.5 days.\n- [x] Deliberate-break gate: restoring the original zero-on-conversion-error handler made all 8 cases of the named invalid-total regression fail (DID NOT RAISE). Restoring the fix returned the parser and WAL tests to 28 passed.\n\n## Validation\n- `python -m pytest tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py tests/test_wal.py -q` — 28 passed.\n- Focused Ruff, Black and production-module mypy checks passed; `git diff --check` passed.\n- Evidence: opener run `20260920T000206Z`, `acceptance-tests.txt`, `deliberate-break.txt`, and `restored-parser-wal-tests.txt`.\n\n<!-- deliberate-break: test=tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py::test_invalid_nonblank_total_raises test-file=tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py break-file=src/counter_risk/parsers/exposure_maturity_schedule.py -->\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:1063 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #1063\n\nCloses #1063\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\n`src/counter_risk/parsers/exposure_maturity_schedule.py:247` is current evidence at current main 7c01963cb4173128c806347e622ed43a08fdcf4a. Current break: a real synthetic workbook with a maturity date and Total=not-a-number parses as total=0.0. The parser catches every numeric-coercion error and replaces it with zero. Its documented zero-fill contract covers blank cells only (`src/counter_risk/parsers/exposure_maturity_schedule.py:226`); silently discarding a malformed leg can bias the downstream WAL.\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [#963](https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/963)\n- [#1022](https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/1022)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] In `src/counter_risk/parsers/exposure_maturity_schedule.py`, raise the existing maturity schedule error for nonblank unparseable amounts instead of replacing numeric conversion failures with zero.\n- [x] In `tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py`, add `test_invalid_nonblank_total_raises`. Add real workbook cases for blank, malformed text, boolean, NaN or Infinity text, and valid accounting amounts; assert malformed rows fail before `src/counter_risk/calculations/wal.py` returns a result.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py -q` passes and collects `test_invalid_nonblank_total_raises`. Blank totals still parse as zero; malformed nonblank totals raise with row and Total-column context; valid accounting values retain their amounts.\n- [x] Deliberate-break gate: temporarily restore the faulty behavior in `src/counter_risk/parsers/exposure_maturity_schedule.py`; `tests/parsers/test_exposure_maturity_schedule.py::test_invalid_nonblank_total_raises` must fail; revert the deliberate break and rerun the named test to pass. Capture both outcomes in the implementation PR.\n- [x] The test exercises the actual production boundary and retains a valid-input control.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Invalid nonblank maturity amounts now produce clear validation errors with worksheet, row, cell, and value details instead of being treated as zero.\n  * Blank maturity amounts continue to be treated as zero.\n  * Valid numeric and accounting-formatted amounts are preserved when calculating weighted average life.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for validation errors, blank values, formatted totals, and weighted average life calculations.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","closingIssuesReferences":[{"id":"I_kwDORPCqTs8AAAABRJ7riw","number":1063,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDORPCqTg","name":"Counter_Risk","owner":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDQ2MzIy","login":"stranske"}},"url":"https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/issues/1063"}],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8Y9vQ","name":"agent:codex","description":"Assign to Codex agent","color":"0e8a16"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8Y-KA","name":"agents:keepalive","description":"Enable keepalive monitoring on PR","color":"1d76db"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8Y-aw","name":"autofix","description":"Let bots format/lint automatically","color":"0366d6"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACX8esvQ","name":"verify:compare","description":"Runs verifier comparison mode after merge","color":"1D76DB"},{"id":"LA_kwDORPCqTs8AAAACpd5UZQ","name":"codex","description":"","color":"ededed"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"1aacdd1f98ec3385dc50cc73d5f37c7138ca5bac"},"mergedAt":"2026-09-20T01:43:54Z","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-20T01:44:02Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/stranske/Counter_Risk/actions/runs/35482152706/job/106001761210","name":"create-new-pr","startedAt":"2026-09-20T01:44:03Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Cr